==Quick Walkthrough==
# Once you've entered [[Skyrim:Sovngarde (place)|Sovngarde]], continue down the path.
# Find out how to defeat [[SR:Alduin|Alduin]].
# Gain admittance to the [[SR:Hall of Valor|Hall of Valor]].
# Talk to the heroes of Sovngarde.

==Detailed Walkthrough==
[[File:SR-quest-Sovngarde 02.jpg|thumb|Inside the Hall of Valor]]
You are transported to a [[Skyrim:Sovngarde (place)|misty realm]] filled with statues of [[Skyrim:Nord|Nord]] warriors. The mist has no noticeable effect on you and can be temporarily cleared with the [[Skyrim:Clear Skies|Clear Skies]] shout, but it quickly rematerializes. Upon continuing down the stone steps, you may be stopped by a [[Skyrim:Stormcloak Soldier (Sovngarde)|Stormcloak soldier]] who says that the mist is extremely dangerous and that you should not go into it. He died fighting the [[Skyrim:Imperial Legion|Imperial Legion]], and all his companions have been swallowed up by the mist, where he says [[Skyrim:Alduin|Alduin]] lurks, devouring souls. He also tells you that at the end of the valley of mist lies [[Skyrim:Hall of Valor|Shor's Hall]], where the heroes of Sovngarde gather. He begs you to allow him to follow you.

True enough, Alduin will periodically swoop in and grab a fallen [[Skyrim:Stormcloaks|Stormcloak]] or Legion soldier in the misty valley. On the way, you may encounter historical figures such as [[Skyrim:High King Torygg|High King Torygg]] and [[Skyrim:Svaknir|Svaknir]], along with NPCs that have died in the course of the game, such as [[Skyrim:Kodlak Whitemane|Kodlak Whitemane]], [[Skyrim:Ulfric Stormcloak|Ulfric Stormcloak]], [[Skyrim:Legate Rikke|Legate Rikke]], or [[Skyrim:Galmar Stone-Fist|Galmar Stone-Fist]]. Once clearing the mist, you'll reach the edge and be stopped by the gate guardian, [[Skyrim:Tsun|Tsun]]. He challenges your right to enter the Hall of Valor and declares that you must prove your worth in a warrior's duel regardless of the right that you claim. The first claim 'by the right of birth' will always appear regardless of what you have done in the game, but the remaining ones can only be used if you have completed the quests of the Companions, the College of Winterhold, the Dark Brotherhood and/or the Thieves Guild, respectively.
